#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/contributor-feedback.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A document is still being written, and the Authoring Committee gives feedback on it in a shared Contributor Feedback sheet. This is what happens to ONE change set, one row of that sheet: a member starts it with a title, the sections it is about and their feedback; the agent proposes a direction; an Editor lets the agent edit; the agent makes the edit in the row's one pull request, whose staging preview shows what changed; the committee answers on the row; and an Editor lets the agent merge. If the row's feedback changes after the agent wrote its proposal, the proposal is marked stale and the row's Ready for agent goes back to No, so the agent proposes again and an Editor decides again. The sheet's colours follow the lanes: Blue for the committee, Green for the agent, Orange for the Editor. Skill: review-sheet-script."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/contributor-feedback.bpmn:72
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A member adds a row on the Contributor Feedback tab: a title, the Selected Sections it is about (a dropdown from the document's table of contents) and their feedback in their own Blue column. The script gives the row its Change-set id and links each section."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/contributor-feedback.bpmn:131
#. Diagram label
msgid "agreed"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/contributor-feedback.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "An Editor agrees the direction and sets the row's Ready for agent (Orange) to Yes. Person-only: the agent never sets it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/contributor-feedback.bpmn:109
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "An Editor sets the row's Ready for merge (Orange) to Yes. Person-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/contributor-feedback.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the script, which compares the row's Blue cells with the basis the agent wrote. `changed`: the proposal is marked stale and Ready for agent goes back to No, so the agent proposes again and an Editor decides again. `agreed`: nothing moved, and the row goes to the merge decision."
msgstr ""

